
cd ~/Juniper

git status

git pull               - Downloads latest updates from GitHub
                         Use BEFORE editing files

git add file1.docx     - Prepares file for commit

git add .              - Adds ALL changed files

git commit -m "Updated Juniper notes" - Saves snapshot locally

git push - Uploads changes to GitHub cloud
           Windows can then pull them

git remote -v         - Shows if repo is connected to GitHub

git log --oneline     - Shows past commits

git ls-files          - Shows files stored in Git history

Common fix commands
If something looks wrong:

git status 

If you forgot upstream branch:

git branch --set-upstream-to=origin/main

ssh -T git@github.com - Confirms login works

----------------------------------------

git rm testfile1.txt         - remove file from git and disk 

git commit -m "Remove file"

git push

----------------------------------------

git rm --cached testfile1.txt   - Remove file from Git BUT keep it on disk

git commit -m "Stop tracking file"

git push

